Package: snpflowR
Title: Directional Genetic Differentiation Signals from Biallelic SNPs
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Pauline", "Owusu-Ansah", email = "paulineowusu653@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates directional genetic differentiation from biallelic
    single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) allele counts using the hypothetical
    migrant-pool construction of Sundqvist et al. (2016)
    <doi:10.1002/ece3.2096>. Provides explicit input checks, auditable locus
    filtering, paired locus or block bootstrap intervals, and reproducible
    neutral simulations. Outputs are exploratory relative gene-flow signals,
    not estimates of absolute migration rates or evidence of contemporary
    migration. Includes diagnostics for unresolved comparisons.
